Q: Saving an OpenXML SpreadsheetDocument to a stream A: <p>Are two <code>MemoryStream</code> really necessary?</p>

<p>Try to flush <code>tempStream</code> before deriving a new <code>MemoryStream</code> from it.
Example:</p>

<pre><code>spreadsheetDocument.WorkbookPart.Workbook.Save(tempStream);
tempStream.Flush();
stream = new MemoryStream(tempStream.ToArray());
</code></pre>

<p>Also, do you save the output to a file or read it from memory? <code>MemoryStream</code>'s content is logically lost as soon as you <code>.Close()</code> it.</p>

